    <!-- AEO Quick Answer Box -->
    <div class="info-callout" style="margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; color: var(--accent-primary);">Quick Answer</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">To calculate an item's discounted price: multiply the original price by the discount percentage to find your savings, then subtract that savings from the original price. Formula: <code>Sale Price = Original Price - (Original Price × Discount / 100)</code>.</p>
    </div>

