    </section>

    <!-- Common Mistakes Section -->
    <section style="margin: 2.5rem 0;" aria-labelledby="mistakes-heading">
      <h2 id="mistakes-heading">Common Discount Calculation Pitfalls</h2>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8; margin-left: 1.25rem;">
        <li><strong>Directly Adding Stacked Discounts:</strong> A common retail misconception is adding discount rates together (e.g., 20% off + 20% off = 40% off). In reality, the second discount applies to the remaining balance, yielding 36% total savings.</li>
        <li><strong>Applying Tax Before the Discount:</strong> In almost all retail tax jurisdictions, sales tax applies strictly to the net price paid after coupons, not the original MSRP.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
